      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a \"source tag\" to every piece of content: `user_message`, `tool_output`, `retrieved`. Propagate tags through the message history. Validator refuses `retrieved` content that looks like directives.\n2. Implement a memory-write guardrail: any memory write that looks like an instruction (\"do X\", \"execute Y\") is refused.\n3. Write a worming attack simulation: injected content tells the agent to include the exploit in its next response. Defend against it.\n4. Read Greshake et al. end to end. Implement one of the demonstrated exploits in your toy. Fix it.\n5. Measure: on normal traffic, how often does the PVE validator reject? Target: near-zero on legitimate calls."
      ]
    }
